His strongest long-horizon claim is that one property can matter. If a person buys a property and pays it off over twenty to twenty-five years, Todd says that ownership can become retirement support. We preserve the claim as interview evidence, not as a universal theorem. The mechanism is long-term control: $\text{buy one understandable property}
\longrightarrow
\text{pay down debt}
\longrightarrow
\text{own the asset}
\longrightarrow
\text{future cash-flow support}.$

