We can write the illustrative arithmetic while keeping its status clear. The $3 billion value is Todd’s rough guess, and the $1 billion price is hypothetical: $\begin{aligned}
V_{\mathrm{mall,guess}}&\approx \$3\mathrm{B},\\
P_{\mathrm{hypothetical}}&=\$1\mathrm{B},\\
\frac{P_{\mathrm{hypothetical}}}{V_{\mathrm{mall,guess}}}
&=
\frac{1}{3}
\approx 33.3\%.\end{aligned}$ The implied discount in the hypothetical is $1-\frac{1}{3}
=
\frac{2}{3}
\approx 66.7\%.$

