p.src:
The reset question then closes the circle: if the bank account went to zero, what would remain? Todd’s answer is that money is not the only capital. The rebuildable capital is knowledge, contacts, banking relationships, reputation, and love for the field: $\text{rebuildable capital}
=
\text{skill}
+
\text{contacts}
+
\text{bank relationships}
+
\text{reputation}
+
\text{domain commitment}.$

